.webp"}],"second":"no","why_by_stat":{"DMGAmp":"Increases all damage dealt by Feng Yan by the given %, making it useful for both general damage and higher PVE scores. Also increases DOT damage."},"story":"\"Can I... start over again?\"\n\nFeng Yan studied the hairpin Soi had given him and reminisced about his days of training in the past. To repay the debt of gratitude to his former Master, Feng Yan sought to protect Soi from harm — but was tormented by a sense of inadequacy and helplessness when he could do nothing to aid Soi as she suffered from a mysterious, raging fever. However, once Soi's condition stabilized with the help of Lina and Evan, Feng Yan reflected upon his shortcomings and stood tall once more, renewed with a fresh sense of determination."},"used_in":[{"tip":"Castle Rush (Thu/Fri/Sat)","cat":"pve","banner":"CR_THURSFRISAT.webp"},{"tip":"Advent Expedition: Karma","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENT_KARMA.webp"},{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon: Water","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON_WATER.webp"},{"tip":"Adventure (Both)","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENTURE_BOTH.webp"},{"tip":"Tower of Trials","cat":"pve","banner":"TOWER_OF_TRIALS.webp"}],"lore":"A sage from Sage Peak.\nHe was moved by his master's quest to collect the Shards of Destruction to save the world with the Power of Destruction, and he endeavors to do the same.\nHe wields flying swords in battle. His incredible strength has earned him the moniker Bladestorm Lord. He is proud of his status as a sage, oftentimes leading others to mistake it for arrogance.\nBack in the day, he attacked Teo to try and take the Shards of Destruction that Teo had collected for Silvesta, but was soundly beaten.\nHis pride and confidence can lead him to overestimate his skills."}